1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,610
Let's take a tour of the PadDeck screen, so you know what every part does.

2
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:11,776
On the left are the sections: Stream Deck, Soundboard, Control Centre, Audio, Apps,

3
00:00:11,776 --> 00:00:13,880
and Settings at the bottom.

4
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:20,091
Across the top are your pages: Home, Work, Gaming, and Creative.

5
00:00:20,091 --> 00:00:22,330
Tap a page name to switch.

6
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:26,517
Next to the connection badge is the current profile.

7
00:00:26,517 --> 00:00:30,540
Tap it to switch to another profile, such as Work or Gaming.

8
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:36,980
The Edit button, at the top right, lets you add, move, and change tiles.

9
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:42,566
At the bottom you have a volume slider, the current speakers or headphones,

10
00:00:42,566 --> 00:00:44,260
and the microphone button.

11
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:50,058
The green Live button at the top is your microphone too: green means people can hear you,

12
00:00:50,058 --> 00:00:51,100
red means muted.

13
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:59,077
On the PC, the sidebar lists Dashboard, Stream Deck Editor, Applications, Soundboard,

14
00:00:59,077 --> 00:01:03,100
Audio Control, Profiles, Devices, and Settings.

